  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Northern Uganda: Transforming the Economy through Climate Smart Agribusiness (NU-TEC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase the resilience to climate change of poor farmers in Northern Uganda, and to increase their incomes.   This will be achieved by working with agricultural businesses to supply farmers with cheaper, better and more varied agricultural inputs and services, and to create stronger markets for farmer produce.  This will benefit 250,000 households in Northern Uganda, who will adopt new practices, products and markets that will make them more resilient to climate change, while 150,000 households will see measurable increases to income. This will contribute to the MDGs (and their successor targets) by reducing poverty in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
